# Image tag deployed per app, recorded by each app repo's release workflow
# (scripts/record-tag.sh) and read by the deploy. Plain text on purpose: these name public
# images, they are not secrets, and the diff of a bump has to be readable.
#
# This file is the source of truth for what runs in production. To roll one app back,
# revert its `chore(deploy): <APP>_TAG=...` commit.
#
# A variable must be declared here BEFORE its app repo can record into it, and only once
# that repo actually publishes the image: docker-compose.yml pins these with
# `${<APP>_TAG:?}`, so declaring one whose image does not exist yet wedges the whole-stack
# deploy, not just that app.
#
# No app is recorded yet. Apps still built by this repo's own release.yml stay on IMAGE_TAG.
